Z||000006||Mach10||11-24-2001||08:44 PM||||hehehe... Welcome! I think the 'vette pictures threw him/her off... Don't worry about it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>On the top right-hand of the screen you will see a "search" function. You can find 95% of your answers right there. Of course, if you don't see what you require, don't hesitate to ask.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Times: I've seen 12s to 16s posted here. <BR>Mods: You name it. It's PROBABLY been done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>F355? Well, "Sweetness" is directly proportional to how much you dump into it... I've seen un-prepped kits go for anywhere from $2000us to $10000US, and everything in between. I'd expect to at least double the kit price to have it look nice, after paint  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>4.9? I wanna do one. There's some quirks with that engine which people are working out... It's easy to do, but not terribly tuneable. There is very little (if any) aftermarket. You can't, for example, find any commercially produced cams  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">... Although I'm still looking  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
